repl_unpin — implementation plan
=================================

status: planned (2026-07-09)

references I1..I5 (plans/repl_list); pin lifecycle owned by
plans/repl_pin. pass-through ("unpin" => keys ["repl"]).

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          repl_unpin
description   "Remove a REPL's pin. Fails if other REPLs were
              initialized from this pin (remove them first, or leave
              the pin in place). Unpinning does not change the REPL's
              own steps or state."
              (source: mcp_server.py repl_unpin :403 + the dependency
              guard of ir.ML:523.)
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {"repl": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["repl"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": false,
               "openWorldHint": false}
              (not idempotent: unpinning an unpinned repl errors.)
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "repl_unpin", {"repl": "A"}
  scala builtin row backend.ir("unpin", [(repl, A)])
  ml dispatcher     "unpin" -> Ir.unpin (get "repl")
  engine            ir.ML:523 — errors on no pin / dependents;
                    out "Unpinned \"A\""

implementation steps
--------------------

1. [this tool] builtin row + handler; errors -> isError.
2. tests; rebuild per rules.

assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

T1  unpinning without a pin is an error naming the repl.
    test [ml unit]: init, unpin -> error "is not pinned".
T2  dependents block: pin A, init B [pin@A], unpin A -> error;
    remove B, unpin A -> ok; A's steps unchanged throughout.
    test [ml unit]: as stated; show A after -> no "pinned", same
    step count.
    NOTE while implementing: has_pin_dep matches on origin SPECS, so
    a dependent still blocks after it rebases (its origin still says
    pin@A) — expected; the test should cover the remove path, not
    hope rebase frees it.
T3  full chain.
    test [bridge]: pin/unpin round trip via session.ir.

done when
---------

- T1..T3 green; tools/list shows the row above.

status: done (2026-07-09). T1..T3 green at all layers. T1 confirmed
